<section class="sec" id="why">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">Why now</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">Why UI/UX design, and <span class="serif">why now.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">Every app and website that frustrates you is a company losing money, and UI/UX designers exist to stop that. India's product boom keeps demand strong, and AI has shifted the job toward what it always should have been: research, judgement and taste.</p>
<div class="why-stats">
<div class="ws reveal"><b>$100</b><span class="t">Return per $1 on UX</span><p>The most-quoted ROI figure in design exists because usability sells.</p></div>
<div class="ws reveal"><b>Product</b><span class="t">India builds, not just codes</span><p>Startups and GCC product teams hire designers, not just developers.</p></div>
<div class="ws reveal"><b>AI</b><span class="t">Raises the taste bar</span><p>AI drafts screens; designers who research and decide become more valuable.</p></div>
</div>
<h3 class="reveal" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:800;font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:44px">Why it is a smart move for you</h3>
<div class="diff-grid" style="margin-top:22px">
<div class="diff reveal"><span class="ic-badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#i-cap"></use></svg></span><b>Research-first training</b><p>You learn to find the real problem before drawing a single screen.</p></div>
