<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>What is the difference between UI/UX and graphic design? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Graphic design communicates messages; UI/UX designs how products work. This course centres research, flows and testing, with visual craft serving usability. Graphic designers who cross over do well here.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do I need to draw or code? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Neither. Figma replaces drawing skill with construction skill, and while we build developer empathy with an HTML/CSS taste module, no coding is required for design roles.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is a portfolio really more important than a certificate? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">In design hiring, decisively yes. Interviews walk through your case studies for an hour. That is why two defended capstones and case-study writing consume the final third of this course.</div></details>
<details><summary>What does a UI/UX designer earn in India? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Juniors typically start between Rs 3 and 5.5 lakh, with product designers reaching Rs 5.5 to 10 within two to three years. GCC and remote product roles push bands higher.</div></details>
<details><summary>Will AI design tools take these jobs? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">AI now drafts screens in seconds, which moves the paid work to research, judgement and system thinking, exactly what this course over-invests in. Designers who only pushed pixels are the ones at risk.</div></details>
<details><summary>Can graphic designers or developers switch through this course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both switch well. Designers arrive with visual craft and add research and product rigour; developers arrive with build empathy and add user thinking. Case studies frame your prior work as an advantage.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala and the GCC. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
</div>
